  "mappingRules": [
    "Arithmetic word problems (ratio, %, profit-loss, ages, time-speed-work, mixtures, averages, interest) -> R-NUM Numerical Reasoning, because NIMCET places them in the Reasoning section.",
    "Clocks & Calendars -> R-NUM Numerical Reasoning (calculation-based).",
    "Cubes, dice, paper folding, counting figures, embedded figures, figure series -> R-FIG Figure-based Reasoning; water images -> R-MIR.",
    "Number/letter series and odd-one-out inside a series -> R-SER.",
    "Grid/ordering/selection/scheduling puzzles -> R-PUZ; linear/circular seating -> R-SEAT.",
    "Truth-teller, implication, 'which must be true' logic -> R-DED; course-of-action / assumption / cause-effect -> R-SCA; strengthen/weaken/inference from passage -> R-CT; multi-step optimisation, weighing, counting logic -> R-PS.",
    "Relations and functions: counting relations, relation properties -> M-SET; domain/range/inverse/composite/periodic/even-odd functions -> M-FUN.",
    "Trig identities and values -> M-TRIG; radian/degree conversion -> M-ANG.",
    "Networking and protocols -> C-WEB (syllabus: 'understanding how the internet works').",
    "Logic gates, K-maps, flip-flop logic -> C-BOOL; number base conversion -> C-BHX; signed number / complement arithmetic -> C-TWC.",
    "Compilers, assemblers, loaders, linkers -> C-SYS; memory hierarchy, addressing, virtual memory, memory units -> C-MEM; specific RAM/ROM/cache types and cache mapping -> C-RRC.",
    "Synonyms, antonyms, idioms, one-word substitution -> E-WPM; fill in the blanks -> E-WU; error spotting/tense/preposition/agreement -> E-GP; sentence improvement, voice, narration -> E-SF; spelling, prefixes/suffixes -> E-WF."
  ]
